IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei2-nouns`
IMPORT `ei2-s23-3-division`

-- Tests of ei2-s23-3-division (s 23.3(6) to (9)). Expected values are written by hand from the text, before
-- running: each comment says which words of the Act give the answer.

§ `s 23.3(6) - how many remaining weeks may be divided`

-- "(6) ... any remaining weeks of benefits payable ... up to a maximum of 15 weeks, may be divided".
-- Both conditions hold and 20 weeks remain: only 15 may be divided.
#ASSERT `s 23.3(6) the number of remaining weeks that may be divided` TRUE TRUE 20 EQUALS 15
-- Exactly 15 remain: all 15 (the boundary, "up to a maximum of 15").
#ASSERT `s 23.3(6) the number of remaining weeks that may be divided` TRUE TRUE 15 EQUALS 15
-- 14 remain: all 14.
#ASSERT `s 23.3(6) the number of remaining weeks that may be divided` TRUE TRUE 14 EQUALS 14
-- None remain: none can be divided.
#ASSERT `s 23.3(6) the number of remaining weeks that may be divided` TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS 0
-- No other claimant has claimed in respect of the same adult: the subsection does not let anything be divided.
#ASSERT `s 23.3(6) the number of remaining weeks that may be divided` TRUE FALSE 10 EQUALS 0
-- The person has not claimed under this section.
#ASSERT `s 23.3(6) the number of remaining weeks that may be divided` FALSE TRUE 10 EQUALS 0

-- "...divided in the manner agreed to by those claimants. If they cannot agree, ... in accordance with the prescribed rules."
#ASSERT `s 23.3(6) the way the remaining weeks are divided` TRUE EQUALS `ei2 divided in the manner the claimants agreed`
#ASSERT `s 23.3(6) the way the remaining weeks are divided` FALSE EQUALS `ei2 divided in accordance with the prescribed rules`

§ `s 23.3(7) - the ceiling of 15 weeks across sections 23.3 and 152.062`

-- "must not exceed 15 weeks": 15 is within, 16 is not, 14 is within.
#ASSERT `s 23.3(7) the total number of weeks divided is within the ceiling` TRUE TRUE 15 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23.3(7) the total number of weeks divided is within the ceiling` TRUE TRUE 16 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23.3(7) the total number of weeks divided is within the ceiling` TRUE TRUE 14 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The subsection applies only where one claimant claims under s 23.3 and another under s 152.062 in respect of
-- the same adult. Otherwise it says nothing about the total: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 23.3(7) the total number of weeks divided is within the ceiling` TRUE FALSE 16 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23.3(7) the total number of weeks divided is within the ceiling` FALSE TRUE 16 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 23.3(8) - no compassionate care benefits in respect of the adult during the s 23.3(3) period`

-- The period of subsection (3) runs from the first day of a week (a Sunday) to the last day of a week (a Saturday).
-- Here: Sunday 1 March 2026 to Saturday 29 August 2026 (26 weeks, enough to test the ends).
`a section 23.3(3) period` MEANS `Period of days` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2026 8 29)

-- Compassionate care benefits (the keel's reason `care or support of a family member`), the same adult, a week in the period.
#ASSERT `s 23.3(8) benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable` `care or support of a family member` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) `a section 23.3(3) period`
-- The last week of the period: its Sunday is 23 August 2026.
#ASSERT `s 23.3(8) benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable` `care or support of a family member` TRUE (YMD 2026 8 23) `a section 23.3(3) period`
-- The week after the period ends begins on Sunday 30 August 2026: benefits are payable again.
#ASSERT NOT `s 23.3(8) benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable` `care or support of a family member` TRUE (YMD 2026 8 30) `a section 23.3(3) period`
-- The week before the period begins (Sunday 22 February 2026).
#ASSERT NOT `s 23.3(8) benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable` `care or support of a family member` TRUE (YMD 2026 2 22) `a section 23.3(3) period`
-- A different reason for benefits: the subsection speaks of sections 23.1 and 152.06 only.
#ASSERT NOT `s 23.3(8) benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable` `pregnancy` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) `a section 23.3(3) period`
-- Benefits claimed in respect of some other person than the adult for whom the period was established.
#ASSERT NOT `s 23.3(8) benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable` `care or support of a family member` FALSE (YMD 2026 3 1) `a section 23.3(3) period`

§ `s 23.3(9) - reduction by a provincial law`

#ASSERT `s 23.3(9) the benefits payable under section 23.3 are to be reduced or eliminated as prescribed` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 23.3(9) the benefits payable under section 23.3 are to be reduced or eliminated as prescribed` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 23.3(9) the benefits payable under section 23.3 are to be reduced or eliminated as prescribed` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 23.3(9) the benefits payable under section 23.3 are to be reduced or eliminated as prescribed` TRUE TRUE FALSE
